WEBVTT

00:00:00.978 --> 00:00:03.897
A robot is about to cross this room.

00:00:04.096 --> 00:00:06.741
There are two places it could be going.

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:08.264
Watch it move.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.787
How soon can you tell which one?

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:13.716
The shortest route keeps you guessing.

00:00:13.973 --> 00:00:16.963
For most of the way, it could be heading
to either.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.410
A legible route gives the answer away
early.

00:00:22.637 --> 00:00:26.517
It swings wide, away from the place it is
not going.

00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:29.093
But that costs extra distance.

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:34.241
Planners search for the clearest route a
budget allows,

00:00:34.191 --> 00:00:36.348
and report the best they found.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.783
Which leaves a question no search can
settle.

00:00:40.008 --> 00:00:42.732
Is this room hard to be clear in?

00:00:42.972 --> 00:00:45.290
Or did the planner just do badly?

00:00:45.181 --> 00:00:47.770
Legibility Bounds answers it.

00:00:48.054 --> 00:00:50.013
The key fact is this.

00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:54.293
What the observer believes depends only on
where the robot is,

00:00:54.243 --> 00:00:56.096
not on how it got there.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.856
So belief is a map of the floor, drawn
once.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.447
And a robot on a budget cannot be just
anywhere.

00:01:03.673 --> 00:01:07.217
Part way along, it must still be near
enough to the start,

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.154
and near enough to the goal.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.947
The best belief inside that region is a
ceiling.

00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:15.825
On every possible route, at once.

00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:19.715
Then it builds a real route to stand
beneath that ceiling.

00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:27.585
Here, with half as much path again to
spend, a route that scores 0.8004 exists.

00:01:27.768 --> 00:01:30.715
And nothing can reach 0.81.

00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:34.742
Eight test worlds, four budgets each.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.614
No bound broken.

00:01:36.864 --> 00:01:42.653
And the same argument puts a certified
price on keeping clear of a safety zone.

00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:45.854
One caution, which the project states
itself.

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:49.111
The observer is a mathematical model.

00:01:49.364 --> 00:01:52.502
It has not yet been tested against people.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:54.199
Legibility Bounds.

00:01:54.381 --> 00:01:57.096
Not just the best a search could find.

00:01:57.308 --> 00:02:00.408
Proof of what is possible, and what is
not.
